<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial Bank dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial Bank of Ceylon Ltd fell 2.2 percent, or 2.50 rupees on Monday to 112.50, on turnover of 500 shares as retailer investors booked profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is profit-taking because investors now know they will get all the rights shares they wanted at 80 rupees each,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank declared a one for four rights issue at 80 rupees earlier this year.</p>
<p>The blue chip bank is one of four commercial banks listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
